# ============================================================================
# Tencent Cloud runtime environment — loaded by pok-evolution.service
# ============================================================================
# This EnvironmentFile turns this checkout into an ISOLATED cloud evolution
# line. The four namespace/branch variables below make commit_bot publish into
# the tencent-cloud-runtime branch with a national_cloud_v tag namespace that
# NEVER collides with origin/main (which keeps the canonical national_v line).
#
# POK_CLOUD_RUNTIME=1 + PROJECT_ROOT.name==".evolution_pok" triggers the
# setdefault block in web/main.py that seeds these same values for direct
# `python web/main.py` launches. Setting them here explicitly is authoritative
# (setdefault never overrides).
# ============================================================================

# --- Publication-branch / namespace isolation (the core of this branch) ---
POK_CLOUD_RUNTIME=1
# Ensure Node.js is on PATH for the --no-build frontend static receipt verifier.
# Use the distro/NodeSource node (`/usr/bin/node`), not an IDE-bundled binary.
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
POK_EVOLUTION_BRANCH=tencent-cloud-runtime
POK_BOT_PREFIX=national_cloud_v
POK_TAG_PREFIX=national-cloud-bot-v
POK_HIGH_WATER_TAG_PREFIX=national-cloud-high-water-v
POK_REAPED_TAG_PREFIX=national-cloud-reaped-v

# --- Publication push semantics (set by the .evolution_pok block too) ---
POK_EVOLUTION_RUNTIME=1
POK_REQUIRE_EVOLUTION_PUSH=1
EVOLUTION_GIT_PUSH=1

# --- Remote publication proof cache TTL (seconds) ---
# Read-only observer requests (/api/bots, /api/control/status|health) re-resolve
# the published pool frequently; with POK_REQUIRE_EVOLUTION_PUSH=1 each cache
# miss runs `git ls-remote origin` against GitHub, which on a constrained link
# can take 30-60s and stall the API. Default 60s keeps the read path off the
# network during a poll burst. Publication/launch boundaries still call
# _clear_remote_publication_cache() to force a fresh proof, so a longer TTL
# does NOT weaken publication validation.
POK_REMOTE_PUBLICATION_CACHE_TTL=60

# --- Python interpreter (MUST be an absolute path; set before first run) ---
# pokctl.sh resolves this automatically; systemd needs it explicit. Point it at
# the interpreter that has web/sever requirements installed.
POK_PYTHON=/home/ubuntu/pok1/.venv/bin/python

# --- Web server ---
PORT=8000
# Bind loopback by default; put a reverse proxy (nginx/caddy) in front for TLS.
# Set to 0.0.0.0 only if the security group + firewall are correctly configured.
HOST=127.0.0.1

# --- Rating daemon sizing (4 vCPU / 3.6 GiB VM) ---
# Native matches are subprocess + TCP I/O bound and do NOT consume LLM
# concurrency slots, but they DO consume CPU. With 3 daemon workers running
# concurrent native matches alongside precommit's 8 matches, the CPU is
# saturated and LLM-launched claude subprocesses get starved — the direct
# cause of low LLM utilization. Reducing to 1 worker leaves CPU headroom for
# LLM work during precommit/rating windows.
# 2026-08-15: measured load 6.94/4 cores with 3 workers (daemon parent ~75% +
# 3 concurrent matches x 2 engines each ~23-70%); lowered 3 -> 1 to bring load
# under ~4.5. Glicko rating periods are save-cycle indices (not wall-clock),
# so a slower match cadence converges ratings ~3x slower but stays
# mathematically valid; the priority-bot scheduling boost and the eval-wait
# degradation fallback are unchanged.
# 2026-09-13: reviewed again during the Master-deadlock repair and KEPT at 1/1:
# LLM utilization is the protected budget on this VM, and per-matchup evidence
# tier annealing (web/core/agent_master_validation.py) already makes the
# current pool citable. Raise only if H2H best-rows stay under the shared
# 15-game floor and `pipeline.master_audit_evidence_floor_unsatisfiable`
# events appear — and then only after re-measuring load with the saturator
# running.
# 2026-10-06 (P2, operator directive ②/③ "负载上限提高一倍——1 分钟 load 可
# 持续 3.0，对局并发在不影响 LLM 产出下动态调整" + "提高并行"): raised 3 -> 6
# as the GOVERNOR CAP only — the load-adaptive governor
# (web/core/elo_daemon_governor.py) now targets a sustainable 1-minute load
# of 3.0 with band [2.5, 3.0] and bounds [1, 6]; the pool may dispatch up to
# 6 concurrent matches but the governor throttles new dispatch down the
# moment load exceeds 3.0 twice (LLM hard protection unchanged: stream
# stall/timeout drops the gate to 1 immediately). POK_DAEMON_WORKERS is NOT
# part of the rating identity runtime_profile (workers/内部选对顺序不在
# evaluation_data_identity 画像; proven byte-identical by
# web/tests/test_elo_daemon_governor.py::
# test_workers_change_keeps_rating_identity_profile_unchanged), so this raise
# does NOT require archive-and-restart. POK_DAEMON_PAIRS stays 1 — it IS
# identity-pinned and must never change at runtime.
POK_DAEMON_WORKERS=6
POK_DAEMON_PAIRS=1

# Rating-daemon monitor tick (seconds). daemon_monitor_thread auto-restarts a
# dead daemon and pushes the dashboard daemon_stats projection; the tick is
# fingerprint-gated on the evidence inputs, so an unchanged projection is not
# rebuilt. Default 30, clamped to [3, 600] — a dead daemon is auto-restarted
# up to one tick later than the old fixed 3s poll. Uncomment to override:
# POK_DAEMON_MONITOR_INTERVAL_SEC=30

# Stability-observation maintenance loop (strict_epoch_projection + git
# summary each tick). 5s was ~1.2% of a core for a read-only health view;
# 20s only delays first-reader fail-closed waits by at most one tick.
POK_STABILITY_OBSERVATION_MAINTENANCE_INTERVAL=20

# Per-source-bot eval-wait timeout. At pairs=1 (~3min/match) reaching the
# 24-game floor takes ~70min, so the old hardcoded 600s (10min) always timed
# out and forced the consecutive-fail degradation to 12 games. Raise to 30min
# so the eval wait can complete at full strength instead of degrading.
POK_DAEMON_EVAL_TIMEOUT_SEC=1800

# --- LLM control plane (GLM via Anthropic-compatible endpoint) ---
# The evolution pipeline calls the LLM (Master/Reviewer/Critic/Workers) through
# claude_agent_sdk, which speaks the Anthropic protocol. GLM exposes an
# Anthropic-compatible endpoint; claude_agent_sdk reads ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL +
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN (the Claude-Code convention). The model id is
# glm-5.3-flash (API code; interactive Claude Code may use glm-5.3-flash[1m]
# in ~/.claude/settings.json). The TOKEN is secret: put the real value in
# env.runtime.local (gitignored), NOT here. This file is committed to git.
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/anthropic
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=PLACEHOLDER_SET_IN_env.runtime.local
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=PLACEHOLDER_SET_IN_env.runtime.local
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash
ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash
ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash
ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash
POK_LLM_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash

# --- Optional: deterministic deck seed for reproducible strength matches ---
# When set, paired H2H matches swap seats with the same seed to isolate skill
# from luck. Leave unset for production entropy.
# POK_NATIVE_BOT_SEED=

# --- Extended thinking (deep reasoning for strong bot strategy output) ---
# GLM-5.3-Flash via the Anthropic-compatible endpoint:
#   * thinking.type only supports enabled. disabled is remapped in
#     _llm_thinking_options (provider either HTTP 400 or silently drops to
#     low-effort thinking). adaptive remains forbidden on this endpoint.
#   * Depth is reasoning_effort / effort (low/high/max). Interactive
#     Claude Code /effort max does not set MAX_THINKING_TOKENS. The SDK
#     maps thinking.budget_tokens to --max-thinking-tokens (fixed budget),
#     which delays first visible text. GLM-5.3* therefore ignores this
#     numeric budget. A non-5.3 model still uses it as enabled+budget.
#   * effort=max is the official coding default and the production depth.
POK_LLM_THINKING_MODE=enabled
POK_LLM_THINKING_BUDGET=64000
POK_LLM_EFFORT=max

# --- Switchable LLM transport base (unset = claude, the default) ---
# POK_LLM_TRANSPORT selects the provider process transport for every
# run_claude_query dispatch (the single LLM chokepoint in web/core):
#   claude (default) — claude_agent_sdk spawn of the Claude Code CLI (current
#                      production path; zero behavior change when unset).
#   codex            — one-shot `codex exec --json --ephemeral -s read-only`
#                      per attempt (adapter: web/core/llm_query_codex.py;
#                      JSONL events are translated to the same SDK message
#                      objects, so metrics/IO/quota-classification contracts
#                      are unchanged). Endpoint/model/wire_api/auth come from
#                      the operator's ~/.codex/config.toml (official GLM
#                      Coding Plan page: base_url
#                      https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/v1, wire_api="responses",
#                      experimental_bearer_token). POK_LLM_EFFORT maps onto
#                      codex model_reasoning_effort (low/high/max).
# Switching is an orchestration decision — the key is intentionally left
# UNSET here (do not uncomment locally without coordinating):
POK_LLM_TRANSPORT=codex
# Optional per-dispatch overrides used only by the codex adapter.
# Binary resolution (resolve_codex_binary): bare names search PATH first,
# then fall back to $HOME/.local/bin (pip --user base — the codex CLI user
# install lives there and the service PATH above does NOT include it), so
# the codex transport works under the committed service environment with no
# extra key (2026-10-04 service-env smoke: HOME/PATH/POK_LLM_TRANSPORT
# alone). POK_CODEX_BIN remains an optional authoritative override — a
# value with a directory component is checked directly with NO fallback
# (absolute path recommended, e.g. /home/ubuntu/.local/bin/codex); a truly
# unresolvable binary fails web lifespan startup with an actionable error
# (2026-10-03: v490/v491 abandoned and v492's master slots lost to per-role
# spawn FileNotFoundError before this guard existed).
POK_CODEX_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash

# --- Global LLM concurrency (producer-consumer model) ---
# All sub-agent LLM calls are capped at this many simultaneous in-flight
# streams via a process-wide asyncio.Semaphore in run_claude_query.
# FIFO ordering prevents starvation; Master/Worker stages are temporally
# separated by the linear pipeline stage machine.
#
# Raised to 4 (2026-08-05): the semaphore is PARTITIONED into consumer
# (gate/review/critic) + producer (Master/Worker/direction) sub-pools.
# total=4 → consumer=max(1,4//3)=1, producer=4-1=3. The consumer lane
# (publication critical path) gets an exclusive permit so it is never starved
# by producer Scout bursts under multi-ahead. The producer lane gets 3 permits,
# which lets all 3 proposal Scouts run simultaneously in ONE round (previously
# total=3 → producer=2 → 3 Scouts queued in 2 rounds, wasting wall-clock).
# The 429-storm risk that previously kept this at 3 is now mitigated by the
# rate_limiter singleton (pauses the whole pipeline on quota exhaustion) and
# the llm_availability durable pause — both absent when the cap was last set.
# The producer/consumer hard partition was removed: all roles now share one
# FIFO semaphore, which roughly doubles real utilization for the same permit
# count (slots no longer sit idle during temporally-separated phases).
#
# Memory-driven cap (2026-08-10): this host is 3.6Gi RAM + 2Gi swap. At 8
# concurrent GLM streams each ~200-300MB RSS, plus bwrap native-match
# subprocesses + the ZCode client (~1.4Gi) + daemon, the box OOM-froze and
# had to be hard-rebooted. 8 also saturated the GLM provider (0-TextBlocks /
# first_activity timeouts under load). Lowered to 4: the pool still stays
# saturated by deep-parallelism drafts without freezing the host.
#
# Memory budget reality (2026-08-10, second OOM-reboot): each GLM stream spawns
# a claude SDK subprocess at ~250MB RSS. The ZCode client occupies ~1.3Gi
# (zcode-host + cli + node-repl + ZCode + zygote + Xorg). At concurrency=4 the
# claude subprocesses alone consume ~1Gi, leaving <700Mi for the pok service
# (600MB) + native matches + OS — the box froze AGAIN. Lowered to 2: claude
# subprocesses now ~500MB, leaving ~1.5Gi headroom for native matches. Deep
# parallelism still fills the native-idle window (drafts queue on the 2 permits).
# 2 × 85% × ~819 tok/s ≈ 5M tok/h, still ~20x the 242K baseline. The binding
# constraint is the ZCode client's 1.3Gi — closing it would allow concurrency=4+.
# 2026-09-12: raised 4 -> 6 together with the daemon-monitor throttle fix (the
# monitor thread no longer re-verifies ~465MB of replay evidence every tick,
# which frees CPU and cuts the heap churn driving main.py growth). 6 is a CAP,
# not a reservation: the saturator still refuses to launch when live `claude`
# children equal the cap or MemAvailable < POK_LLM_SATURATOR_MIN_FREE_MB, so
# actual occupancy stays memory-gated. 2026-09-13: 6 -> 8 on measured headroom
# (cgroup 1792MB@6 + ~235MB/stream), then REVERTED to 6 the same day: the 8th
# permit rarely launched (saturator 800MB guard) and steady state was 7/8 with
# cgroup ~2.2G against MemoryHigh=2400M and load spikes >6. Operator direction:
# raise PER-STREAM efficiency (heavier saturator packet inputs), not
# concurrency. 2026-10-07: 9 -> 12 on measured headroom. 2026-10-20: 12 -> 14
# with the codex-transport stream-RSS correction below (250 -> 130MB, real
# measured 110-115MB/stream). 2026-10-21 (解限流): 14 -> 16 — 16 streams
# ≈ 16×130MB ≈ 2.1G + ~0.6G base = 2.7G against memory.high 2700MiB, with
# memory.max 3500MiB as the OOM-kill buffer (crossing high only throttles);
# the cgroup gradient gate (hard 300MB / soft 150MB / RSS-charged band) and
# the transport-children count bound AIMD's probes toward 32 by MACHINE
# state, not by this static number. AIMD (dynamic, provider-disciplined)
# still owns the effective limit, so this only widens its ceiling headroom.
# Publication-drought breaker (2026-10-23): consecutive terminal abandons above
# the published high-water that force a structural crossover to escape the
# parity-plateau mode-selection deadlock (generation_scheduler.py
# _publication_drought_length). 4 = break after 4 output-free generations; 0 = off.
POK_CROSSOVER_DROUGHT_BREAKER=4

POK_GLOBAL_LLM_CONCURRENCY=16

# --- AIMD dynamic-capacity pacing (2026-10-21 解限流) ------------------------
# The CODE defaults in web/core/llm_concurrency.py ARE these aggressive
# values; the explicit exports pin the production posture against future
# default drift. MIN 2 -> 8: storms used to unload the pool to 2 permits and
# the recovery crawl took 17-25 min while permits idled; 8 keeps the
# post-storm baseline at half the static cap (the deployed learned level
# 5-6 is re-floored UP to 8 at the next process start by _aimd_load's
# clamp). Recovery pace 30s/step below the static cap and probe pace 60s
# above it (was 90/300). Downshift discipline UNCHANGED — 3 failures inside
# the 300s window, step -max(2, limit//4), ceiling 32 — and the floor is
# clamped to POK_GLOBAL_LLM_CONCURRENCY at import so a lone MIN export can
# never split the controller's floor from its fail-open recovery limit.
# 2026-10-23 (audit policy-2): floor raised 8 -> 16 (= the static tested
# capacity). AIMD downsizes the SHARED pool, so an 8 floor let shared-account
# 1302 pressure (external, environmental) squeeze the PIPELINE's own total
# concurrency to half the tested capacity — against the supply-first
# mandate. With floor=static, downshifts still shed probe surplus (32 -> 16)
# but never go below the OOM-tested baseline; RAM gates (cgroup gradient,
# transport-children, MemAvailable) still bound fill launches at request time.
# 2026-10-29 REVERTED 16 -> 8: the static floor disabled AIMD exactly where
# it exists. After two true 1308 exhaustions today the account entered a deep
# throttle posture (~4 admitted prompts/h); floor=16 then livelocked: every
# 90s the pipeline launched its ensemble + the fill lane kept 16 streams,
# every dispatch died on 1302 BEFORE producing (pause occurrences=30,
# 19 rate-preempt waves, ZERO completed sessions for 20+ minutes, v638 stuck
# at direction_audited). Failed launches earn nothing: in the throttle regime
# throughput = successful sessions, and a lower floor serializes launches
# until sessions actually complete. When the account recovers, the unchanged
# raise pacing (60s/30s fast) probes back to the static ceiling 16 on its
# own — the floor only binds during storms.
POK_LLM_AIMD_MIN_LIMIT=8
POK_LLM_AIMD_RAISE_INTERVAL_SEC=60
POK_LLM_AIMD_FAST_RAISE_INTERVAL_SEC=30
# The remaining knobs stay at their (unchanged) code defaults; available for
# future tuning: POK_LLM_AIMD_MAX_LIMIT=32, POK_LLM_AIMD_WINDOW_SEC=300,
# POK_LLM_AIMD_FAILURE_THRESHOLD=3, POK_LLM_AIMD_RAISE_MIN_SUCCESSES=4.

# Saturator-local cap on the 1302/bare-429 frequency backoff (2026-10-21
# 解限流): the fill lane's OWN pause is clamped at 30s instead of riding the
# shared curve to its 120s ceiling, so a storm tail no longer idles the lane
# for two minutes after the durable pause has cleared. The shared curve
# itself (min(120, 8*2**(n-1)) in llm_availability) is UNTOUCHED and remains
# the pipeline durable-pause authority — 管线可用性语义零变化. The knob floors
# at the curve base 8s: it can never cancel the backoff. Storm cost is
# process churn on ~0-token 429 rejections, still bounded by the durable
# pause entry check in run_claude_query and the 15s failure-log limiter.
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_RATE_LIMIT_PAUSE_CAP_SEC=30

# 5h quota pacing (2026-10-10, w2/w4/w5 zero-hour root cause): GLM 1308 caps
# usage over a rolling ~5h window (~178M tokens observed window capacity).
# Unpaced burn ran 16-40M tok/h (avg ~34M/h) — front-loading each window,
# punching through the cap, and the resulting provider-quota pause then
# legitimately zeroed EVERY lane for the window tail (whole 0-token hours:
# 10-08 18:42-19:55, 10-09 14-16, 10-10 00:24-01:57). The saturator now
# clamps its mean opportunistic rate to budget/window = 150M/18000s =
# 30M tok/h: still above the 20M/h hourly KPI, ~84% of the observed cap,
# so the window tail no longer collapses. Pipeline roles (Master/Workers/
# gates) are never gated. Budget 0 disables the pacer entirely.
# 2026-10-11 operator decision: 『宁要高峰、接受配额死小时』 — prefer peak
# throughput and accept the quota-dead tail hours over a paced 30M/h mean.
# Budget set to 0, which DISABLES the pacer entirely (see
# _quota_window_budget_tokens in web/core/llm_concurrency.py: budget<=0 →
# opportunistic_blocked_scale always None). The dual-caliber snapshot fields
# on pipeline.llm_quota_exceeded_detected events are still emitted (they are
# independent of pacing) and remain the calibration source for setting
# POK_LLM_QUOTA_CACHE_WEIGHT should the pacer ever be re-enabled.
POK_LLM_QUOTA_WINDOW_BUDGET_TOKENS=0
POK_LLM_QUOTA_WINDOW_SEC=18000
# Quota-wait provider probing (2026-10-18): while a trusted 1308 block holds,
# one minimal 1-token request every POK_QUOTA_PROBE_INTERVAL_SEC; a single
# acceptance resumes the block AND the durable availability pause ahead of the
# declared reset (observed: the provider re-opened hours before its timestamp).
POK_QUOTA_PROBE_ENABLED=1
POK_QUOTA_PROBE_INTERVAL_SEC=300

# Bounded saturator fill while the orchestrator crash supervisor has a
# revival SCHEDULED (w3 residual ①, 2026-10-10): the pipeline heartbeat is
# stale during every backoff / slow-retry sleep, and the old hard coupling
# parked the background lane for the whole wedge (3h08m zero dispatch on
# 10-09 while revivals were scheduled the entire time). While a revival is
# pending, at most this many saturator packets may be in flight — permits/
# RAM/cgroup/quota-pacing gates still apply. 0 restores the old hard park.
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_RESTART_FILL_INFLIGHT=1

# Saturator cgroup-headroom soft band (2026-10-10, w6; RSS-aware 2026-10-11):
# graduated gate — headroom in [SOFT_FLOOR, 300MB) is a bounded low-memory
# lane admitting at most LOW_MEMORY_INFLIGHT packets; below the floor refuses
# as before. 2026-10-10 deployed the lane DORMANT (inflight=0): one claude
# child is ~200-300MB RSS, so a bare band admission would overshoot a
# 150-300MB band straight past MemoryHigh into kernel-reclaim throttle.
# 2026-10-11 closes that objection with stream-RSS-aware admission in
# llm_saturator.saturator_may_launch:
#   admit(in band)  <=>  headroom - STREAM_RSS_MB >= SOFT_FLOOR_MB - OVERSHOOT_MB
# i.e. the admitted stream's own RSS is charged BEFORE the lane opens, and
# any dip below the soft floor (potentially past MemoryHigh) is explicitly
# capped by OVERSHOOT (0 = no dip allowed). With the committed values below
# (150 / 250 / 0) the line is headroom >= 400 > hard floor 300, so the band
# admits NOTHING under defaults — the observed w6 203-252MB range all refuses
# with the typed `low_memory_cgroup_stream_rss` reason, exactly the dormant
# posture but armed. LOW_MEMORY_INFLIGHT is therefore flipped to 1 (safe: no
# band admission is reachable until an operator deliberately raises
# POK_LLM_SATURATOR_BAND_OVERSHOOT_MB, which is the single explicit
# "how far past MemoryHigh" dial). Worked examples of that dial: OVERSHOOT=150
# admits from headroom >= 250 (post-launch headroom >= 0, touches MemoryHigh
# but never crosses); OVERSHOOT=197 admits from headroom >= 203, the bottom of
# the w6 range, with at most 47MB past MemoryHigh.
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_MEMORY_SOFT_FLOOR_MB=150
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_LOW_MEMORY_INFLIGHT=1
# Per-admission stream RSS charge. 2026-10-20 correction: the 250MB figure was
# measured in the CLAUDE-transport era; on POK_LLM_TRANSPORT=codex each stream
# is a codex exec child measured at 110-115MB RSS (ps over 6 live streams).
# The stale 250MB charge pushed the admission line to headroom >= 400MB
# (250+150 soft floor), parking the saturator lane for whole windows
# ("launch refused: low_memory_cgroup") while real per-stream cost left over
# half the headroom unused. 130 = measured + ~15% margin.
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_STREAM_RSS_MB=130
# Explicit cap on how far a band admission may dip below the soft floor /
# cross MemoryHigh. 0 = never (committed).
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_BAND_OVERSHOOT_MB=0

# --- glibc heap countermeasures (2026-10-11, rss-steps-never-fall-back) ---
# pok-evolution.service loads THIS file via EnvironmentFile=, so process-launch
# glibc tunables belong here (NOT Environment= in the unit; EnvironmentFile
# values reach the ExecStart process env the same way).
#
# MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2: glibc defaults to 8 arenas per core => 32 arenas on this
# 4-vCPU VM. Each thread that needs an arena can pin its own heap, and freed
# chunks inside a thread arena are rarely returned to the OS — the main
# suspect for the observed RSS step pattern that never falls back (the
# service hosts many thread pools: saturator dispatch, observer singleflight
# workers, disk janitor, asyncio default executor). Capping arenas at 2
# bounds that residue; contention cost is negligible for this mostly-I/O
# process. Inherited by python children (elo_daemon, native match workers) —
# they are near-single-threaded, so the cap is harmless there. Node/claude
# and rust/codex children ignore the var.
MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2
# Selective malloc_trim(0) driven from the memory heartbeat's 1s tick
# (web/core/malloc_trim.py + server/app.py). 0 (default) = off. >0 = trim at
# that period in seconds; e.g. 1800 = one libc malloc_trim(0) every 30 min to
# hand free top-of-heap pages back to the kernel between bursts. Any libc
# without malloc_trim, or any ctypes failure, degrades silently. Enable only
# after observing whether MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2 alone flattens the rss stairs
# (watch `journalctl -t pok-evolution | grep pok.memory`).
POK_MALLOC_TRIM_INTERVAL_SEC=0

# Combined-analyst prepare-phase retries. Default 1: logs (2026-08-10) proved 3
# retries never recovered GLM 0-TextBlock storms (33 dispatches still collapsed
# to safe_default), and the inter-attempt sleep(30/60) was pure waste that
# multiplied the LLM queue depth. One attempt + fast safe-default unblocks
# prepare. 429/quota still bubbles via LLMAvailabilityBlocked (re-raised).
POK_COMBINED_ANALYST_MAX_ATTEMPTS=1

# Cross-cycle livelock circuit breaker. If the orchestrator yields N consecutive
# active-checkpoint cycles stuck at the SAME (version, stage) without progress,
# force a canonical abandon (infrastructure_exhausted: reason, admitted at every
# disposable stage). Bounds the directive-path livelock class (v170 spun 36h).
# Healthy generations advance stages and reset the counter, so 5 is safe.
POK_ACTIVE_CKPT_CYCLE_BREAKER=5

# Multi-ahead: allow N concurrent draft preparations alongside the consumer.
# Deep-parallelism (2026-08-10): the REAL throttle on draft creation/sealing is
# now the GLOBAL LLM semaphore (llm_semaphore_has_capacity), NOT this count.
# Drafts are launched/sealed only when LLM permits are free, so the pool stays
# saturated without over-launching.  POK_SLICE2B_MAX_AHEAD is retained only as a
# generous BACKSTOP hard-cap (default 32) to bound disk/checkpoint growth if the
# capacity predicate ever disagrees with reality.  Set it lower only to debug.
POK_SLICE2B_MAX_AHEAD=32

# Native precommit concurrency limiter (deep-parallelism OOM safety valve).
# run_precommit_eval drives native 70-hand TCP matches that consume CPU+RAM but
# ZERO LLM permits.  With deep parallelism, multiple precommits could run in
# parallel and OOM the host (observed SIGKILL rc=-9 on this 3.6Gi VM).  This
# bounds simultaneous precommit chains.  Default 1 (serial) is the safe value;
# raise to 2 only if free -h shows sustained >=2Gi available.  Crucially, when
# this is exhausted the dispatcher returns native_precommit_slot_busy backpressure
# WITHOUT blocking LLM work (other drafts' review/critic keep running).
POK_NATIVE_PRECOMMIT_CONCURRENCY=1

# Backoff (seconds) between native-slot-busy retries in the consumer gate loop.
POK_NATIVE_BACKOFF_SECONDS=30

# Consumer infra-retry budget: how many times the consumer retries a gate that
# reports infrastructure_failure before rejecting the candidate. Default 5
# caused 80+ min zero-LLM precommit loops when native TCP matches hit transport
# stalls (classified as infra, not regression, so they bypass MAX_PRECOMMIT_RETRIES).
# Reducing to 2 caps the infra-retry window at ~2*backoff before the candidate
# is rejected and the system moves to the next generation.
POK_SLICE2B_CONSUMER_INFRA_RETRY_BUDGET=2

# --- Role timeout overrides (generous for GLM variable output speed) ---
# gen-1 typical: Scouts 4-9 min (240-540s). But GLM output speed varies with
# provider load; during peak hours a Scout can take 15-20 min. Since this is
# a non-urgent evolution run (not peak hours), timeouts are kept generous to
# avoid killing GLM mid-reasoning. The stall gate (productive-message silence)
# is the primary stuck-stream detector; total is the hard backstop.
POK_LLM_MASTER_PROPOSAL_STALL_TIMEOUT=1200
POK_LLM_MASTER_PROPOSAL_IDLE_TIMEOUT=1800
POK_LLM_MASTER_PROPOSAL_TOTAL_TIMEOUT=3600
POK_LLM_MASTER_STALL_TIMEOUT=1200
POK_LLM_MASTER_IDLE_TIMEOUT=1800
POK_LLM_MASTER_TOTAL_TIMEOUT=3600
POK_LLM_MASTER_FINAL_STALL_TIMEOUT=1200
POK_LLM_MASTER_FINAL_IDLE_TIMEOUT=1800
POK_LLM_MASTER_FINAL_TOTAL_TIMEOUT=3600
POK_LLM_REVIEW_STALL_TIMEOUT=1200
POK_LLM_REVIEW_IDLE_TIMEOUT=1800
POK_LLM_REVIEW_TOTAL_TIMEOUT=3600
POK_LLM_CRITIC_STALL_TIMEOUT=1200
POK_LLM_CRITIC_IDLE_TIMEOUT=1800
POK_LLM_CRITIC_TOTAL_TIMEOUT=3600
POK_LLM_WORKER_STALL_TIMEOUT=1200
POK_LLM_WORKER_IDLE_TIMEOUT=1800
POK_LLM_WORKER_TOTAL_TIMEOUT=3600
# first_activity must align with GLM effort=max long thinking: only
# SystemMessage(thinking) does NOT count as substantive activity, so the
# legacy Scout/Master default of 120s kills streams mid-reasoning and looks
# like "LLM truncation". Keep these below stall but far above typical
# thinking-only warmup.
POK_LLM_MASTER_PROPOSAL_FIRST_ACTIVITY_TIMEOUT=900
POK_LLM_MASTER_FIRST_ACTIVITY_TIMEOUT=900
POK_LLM_MASTER_FINAL_FIRST_ACTIVITY_TIMEOUT=1200
POK_LLM_REVIEW_FIRST_ACTIVITY_TIMEOUT=900
POK_LLM_CRITIC_FIRST_ACTIVITY_TIMEOUT=900
POK_LLM_WORKER_FIRST_ACTIVITY_TIMEOUT=900
# Crossover is its own policy bucket; without these it inherited the
# generic [60,180]s stall clamp and GLM effort=max died at 180s (v334/v335
# crossover_llm_exhausted). Align with Master/Worker.
POK_LLM_CROSSOVER_STALL_TIMEOUT=1200
POK_LLM_CROSSOVER_IDLE_TIMEOUT=1800
POK_LLM_CROSSOVER_TOTAL_TIMEOUT=3600
POK_LLM_CROSSOVER_FIRST_ACTIVITY_TIMEOUT=900
# DEFAULT covers analysis/probe roles (COMBINED ANALYST, DIRECTION AUDITOR,
# MATCH ANALYST, literature probes) that have no role-specific key. Under GLM
# effort=max these can think >240s before first visible activity; the former
# 240s default killed COMBINED ANALYST mid-reasoning (first_activity timeout),
# causing spurious infra-retry. Raise to 900s to match the gate roles.
POK_LLM_DEFAULT_FIRST_ACTIVITY_TIMEOUT=900
POK_LLM_DEFAULT_IDLE_TIMEOUT=1800
POK_LLM_DEFAULT_TOTAL_TIMEOUT=3600
# Mid-loop stall ceiling for DEFAULT-bucket roles. The code default clamps
# stall to [60,180]s (idle*0.55), which kills GLM effort=max sessions that
# legitimately think 200-500s between productive messages (the same class of
# kill that destroyed 5,944 saturator sessions on 2026-08-14 before SATURATOR
# got its own bucket). Align the stall ceiling with the generous first/idle
# intent above; a genuinely hung stream is still caught by idle (1800s) and
# total (3600s).
POK_LLM_DEFAULT_STALL_TIMEOUT=600

# Orchestrator main-agent stream stall ceiling. The default (300s) cancels the
# main stream whenever a sub-role (Master/Worker) goes >300s without a message
# -- but under GLM effort=max a sub-role routinely thinks 400-900s between
# visible messages, so the 300s default cancelled healthy Master ensembles mid-
# reasoning (orchestrator_stream_stall_timeout at 240-300s silence), restarting
# the whole Master ensemble and wasting LLM budget. Raise it to match the role
# stall timeouts (1200s); the ceiling is still extended by current-generation
# sub-role progress events, so it only fires on genuine total silence.
POK_ORCH_STREAM_STALL_TIMEOUT=1200

# Producer-consumer dual-line activation (Slice 2b one-ahead-buffer).
# RE-ENABLED 2026-08-01: defect E (b) Phase 2 -- FROZEN-SNAPSHOT ISOLATION.
# The consumer gate chain (quality/review/critic/precommit) previously read/
# wrote the LIVE primary pipeline_state.json while the primary lane was parked,
# racing the primary's own reads. Fix: at seal time the consumer slot
# (pipeline_state_consumer-<candidate_id>.json) is seeded with a FULL copy of
# the primary checkpoint, and the entire gate chain runs under
# active_slot_override(consumer_slot) so every no-slot_id checkpoint I/O call
# targets the isolated file. At promotion the consumer slot is CAS-collapsed
# back onto the primary so commit_bot sees the consumer's evidence. The
# consumer_checkpoint_slot id is persisted on the CandidateLifecycle so
# recover_at_boot re-enters the same override after a restart. Prior fixes
# (2026-07-31) remain: seal reuses the producer/worker journal run_id;
# request_effect's status gate is narrowed by effect kind; the validation
# ledger is a PERSISTED CandidateLifecycle FSM (slice2b_lifecycle.sqlite3).
# See docs/slice2b-one-ahead-fsm-2026-07-31.md.
# DISABLED 2026-08-15: with the LLM saturator online (3 deep duel streams
# filling the permits independently of the pipeline), the draft lane's
# original purpose — filling idle LLM capacity — is obsolete, while its
# empty version-reservation registry keeps colliding drafts with the primary
# (snapshot stampede v177-v183, DRAFT_PREIMAGE_CLEARED loops, and the
# prepared->selected checkpoint write fights on v184). Serial primary
# generations + saturator is simpler and strictly better for both goals
# (bot throughput + LLM utilization). Re-enable only after
# draft_version_reservation is fixed to allocate distinct versions.
POK_SLICE2B_ENABLED=0

# LLM saturator: background packets that fill free LLM permits, decoupled
# from the (bursty/stall-prone) pipeline. Jobs rotate matchup / line-audit /
# function-trace and hard-stop at 18 Read turns. MAX_INFLIGHT=6 matches the
# raised GLOBAL cap: it fills every idle permit even if a pipeline role is
# queued. Preempt when the pool is
# full and demand has lasted PREEMPT_AFTER_SEC (15s). Yield at most `waiting`
# packets; leftover ensemble demand (waiting>=2) still yields during the
# 20s cooldown. After a yield wave, HOLDOFF_SEC blocks refill so FIFO
# pipeline waiters take the freed permits (v328-v335: 90s cooldown + same-tick
# refill starved Master scouts and crossover).
# Launch also refuses when live `claude` children already equal the permit
# cap or MemAvailable < MIN_FREE_MB.
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_ENABLED=1
# 2026-10-21 operator directive: do not clamp LLM consumption; let the
# provider quota burn early. The saturator may use the entire global permit
# pool (16) when pipeline roles are idle; the provider's 1302/1308 response
# and AIMD remain the only dynamic bound. The old 8 -> 4 conservation cap is
# removed. Memory guard: MIN_FREE_MB below still refuses a launch when the
# host is truly out of headroom; raise GLOBAL only with memory monitoring.
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_MAX_INFLIGHT=16
# Per-packet Read-call budget. Per-turn cache re-reads dominate saturator
# consumption (web/core/llm_saturator.py::_saturator_bots docstring), so this
# is the PER-STREAM efficiency dial: 18 -> 28 (2026-09-13, operator direction
# is heavier packets instead of higher concurrency), 28 -> 40 (2026-10-07:
# zero 1302/1308 in the preceding 3h at 205 streams and max semaphore wait 0s,
# so the provider is not the binding constraint; heavier packets raise the
# saturator-only windows' floor). Keep TOTAL_TIMEOUT (7200s)
# and STALL_TIMEOUT (600s) above what the raised budget implies.
# 2026-10-28: 40 -> 64 together with the wider packet scope (matchup reads
# FOCUS + OPPONENT + 3 lineage peers, line_audit/function_trace read FOCUS +
# 2 peers). The observed per-packet read distribution before this change was
# p50 15 / p90 26 / max 34, i.e. the old cap was NOT binding — the packets
# simply stopped early. The cap is headroom for the wider scope, not the lever;
# the lever is the required evidence protocol in _SATURATOR_PROMPT.
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_MAX_READ_CALLS=144
# Fill ceiling while PIPELINE LLM streams are in flight (2026-10-27).
# Code default 2 was set on 2026-10-23 to keep the account's request budget
# free for the producer, but the measured effect is a supply hole: with one
# Master/Worker stream open, fill is capped at 2, so the whole service runs
# 3 concurrent streams at ~25 M/h while the account admits 16 permits and
# shows zero 1302. Pipeline time is 22% of the last 24 h (7.25 of 116
# stream-hours), so this cap costs roughly 0.2 x 24 h x 30 M/h. 6 keeps the
# producer's headroom (permits, AIMD floor 16 and the cgroup gates are
# unchanged) while letting the fill lane use the free permits; the
# 2026-10-23 rate-yield preemption still cancels fill when the pipeline
# actually waits for a permit.
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_PIPELINE_ACTIVE_INFLIGHT=12
# Native match workers the load governor may never go below (2026-10-28).
# Default 1 is the historical "yield every core to the LLM streams" posture.
# Measured: the account is PROMPT-rate bound (61-66 admitted prompts/hour with
# ~50 rejected), so CPU yielded to the streams buys no extra prompts, while the
# single worker costs real output -- the rating daemon completes one match per
# ~8-minute cycle (save_cycle re-validates the whole replay corpus), so a new
# bot needs ~3 h to reach the 24-game eval_wait floor before the next
# generation can even prepare. 2 halves that stall.
POK_GOVERNOR_MIN_WORKERS=2
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_PREEMPT_AFTER_SEC=15
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_PREEMPT_COOLDOWN_SEC=20
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_PREEMPT_HOLDOFF_SEC=15
# Last-resort OOM guard, not a throughput cap (2026-10-21): 300MB lets the
# saturator fill the 16-permit pool while still stopping before the cgroup
# MemoryMax. Do not raise this to re-clamp consumption.
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_MIN_FREE_MB=300
# Quality-rework workers run against a hard contract (Opponent Modeler et al).
# The former 600s ceiling was a death sentence under CPU load: v184's
# rework worker timed out 12/12 times over 2h (worker_infrastructure_exhausted
# abandon) while the normal WORKER_TIMEOUT is 1800s. Align the rework ceiling
# with the normal one.
POK_WORKER_QUALITY_REWORK_TIMEOUT=1800
# Saturator deep-research sessions run GLM effort=max with a 64k thinking
# budget; the generic 180s stall clamp killed every deep session mid-thought
# (2026-08-14: 5,944 stall-killed vs 9 completed). SATURATOR has its own
# policy bucket now; these overrides keep the tuning in operator hands.
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_FIRST_ACTIVITY_TIMEOUT=900
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_IDLE_TIMEOUT=900
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_STALL_TIMEOUT=600
POK_LLM_SATURATOR_TOTAL_TIMEOUT=7200

# Disk janitor (process lifetime, independent of orchestrator health).
# Reaps saturator transcripts, orphan draft_candidates, abandoned results/vN
# trees, stale consumer checkpoints, and tmp files. Never truncates
# events.jsonl / abandon ledger / ratings / match_history / live checkpoint.
# When free space on the results filesystem drops below MIN_FREE_GB, retention
# tightens (fewer saturator sessions and abandoned result trees).
POK_DISK_HYGIENE_ENABLED=1
POK_DISK_HYGIENE_INTERVAL_SEC=300
POK_DISK_MIN_FREE_GB=4

# Automatic diagnostic manifests for abandoned precommit failures
# (web/core/diagnostic_manifest.py, started from the web lifespan). Read-only
# scan of precommit_reports/ plus one abandon-transaction receipt walk; writes
# only diagnostics/v<N>/manifest.json once the quarantine exists.
POK_DIAGNOSTIC_MANIFEST_ENABLED=1
POK_DIAGNOSTIC_MANIFEST_INTERVAL_SEC=120

# --- Disk-governance retention (2026-10-21) ---------------------------------
# All knobs below are read by the janitor (web/core/disk_hygiene.py) at its
# call sites; library defaults elsewhere are untouched. The destructive steps
# (retired-identity purge, abandon-txn reap, events auto-rotation) additionally
# require the janitor safe window: no active handoff claim, stage in
# {selected, prepared, crossover_running, direction_audited} (or no live
# checkpoint), no live-ahead draft, plus the disk tier below.
# POK_DISK_TIGHT_FREE_GB=6: below this the purge/reap steps become eligible
# at their default windows (retired 7d / txn 30d); below POK_DISK_MIN_FREE_GB
# (critical) they tighten to 1d/7d and identity keep caps at 4.
POK_DISK_TIGHT_FREE_GB=6
# Identity snapshots (archive/evaluation_identity, measured 8 dirs / ~452M on
# 2026-10-21) keep the newest N; older ones only STAGE into
# archive/evaluation_identity_retired (no bytes freed until the purge below).
# 4 stages ~149M for purge after the 7-day stability window; the library
# default stays 20 for the migration writer itself. Clamp >= 1.
POK_EVALUATION_IDENTITY_KEEP_SNAPSHOTS=4
# Purge retired identity snapshots only after their retention receipt is this
# old (a live-reference re-check runs fail-closed before every purge). The
# critical tier overrides this to 1 day.
POK_IDENTITY_RETIRED_PURGE_AFTER_DAYS=7
# Reap receipt-complete quarantine abandon transactions below the version
# floor after this age (receipt-first into reaped_abandon_transactions.jsonl;
# the abandon ledger itself is never touched; measured 2026-10-21: 397 dirs /
# 76.2M older than 30d). The critical tier overrides this to 7 days.
POK_ABANDON_TXN_RETENTION_DAYS=30
# Workflow journal store (events.sqlite3 + artifacts) retention. Code default
# is 30; 7 bounds the workflow-root growth (measured 164M with all runs <7d
# already clean) and is also the steward's hard lower bound. Pure env change:
# workflow_journal_hygiene.py has read this key since its introduction.
POK_WORKFLOW_JOURNAL_RETENTION_DAYS=7
# Events auto-compression (gzip cold prefix + digest-proven re-head, A-track
# autonomous entry): enabled 2026-10-21. It runs only at the critical tier
# inside an open safe window; a missing entry degrades to
# skipped:"unavailable". The 1800s rebase interval replaces the 6h library
# default because measured events growth is ~55MB/h and a 6h pass cannot keep
# the cold backlog bounded.
POK_EVENTS_AUTO_ROTATION_ENABLED=1
POK_EVENTS_REBASE_MIN_INTERVAL_SEC=1800
# Replay orphan floor (seconds): a replay file unreferenced by live history /
# cycles / verified snapshots is deleted only past this age, because the save
# path writes the file before appending its history row. Leave unset for the
# 3600s default.
# POK_REPLAY_ORPHAN_MIN_AGE_SEC=3600

# Pool-ratchet publication model (2026-10). Unset/absent = legacy (code fallback):
# parent gate only, reap target MAX_ACTIVE_BOTS=30.
# Rollback: comment out or delete POK_PUBLISH_MODE -> legacy.
# N lower bound 12 = _MIN_CROSSOVER_POOL_SIZE (crossover diversity floor).
# Optional per-plan-frozen gate overrides (code defaults shown; leave unset):
# POK_POOL_GATE_MIN_SAMPLES=6 / POK_POOL_GATE_MAX_SCORE=0.50 / POK_POOL_GATE_TIE_CI_LOWER_MIN=0.0
POK_PUBLISH_MODE=pool_ratchet
POK_POOL_RATCHET_TARGET_SIZE=15
# Queue #3 (2026-10-30): tier-0 measured-strength sample floor for the
# pool-weakest gate key AND the reap measured-strong protection set (both
# resolve it at their plan-build moments, never mid-deck — an in-flight
# generation's frozen deck is untouched).  At 600 the tier-0 population was
# ONE bot for 29 consecutive generations (v173 monopoly, block-30 pool audit):
# the admission gate re-tested the same fixed opponent forever because a new
# entrant needs ~4.5 days of daemon play to reach 600 games while the ratchet
# keeps the pool young.  300 halves that wait; the Wilson-95% half-width at
# p~.47 grows from ~0.038 to ~0.055 — still far inside the discrimination
# band between v173 (0.4651) and the mid-pool — and the fail-safe direction
# is unchanged (a wrong pick targets a too-strong member, lowering the
# admission rate, never nominating a measured-weaker member as the bar).
# Code default 600 = the 2026-10-16 calibration; valid range [100, 600] with
# fail-fast on anything else (explicit blocker, never a silent fallback).
# 100 is the floor DELIBERATELY: below it a measured-STRONG member can draw a
# low bound and be nominated "weakest" — the 2026-10-16 v11 bug this tier
# exists to kill.
POK_POOL_WEAKEST_MIN_GAMES=300
# Queue #4 (2026-10-30): outcome-weighted direction veto (the W6
# attempt-counting window repeatedly re-admitted symbols that died at the
# native gates — v641/_candidate_raise_fractions had 3 precommit-breaker
# deaths v630/634/641 while its W6 count read 0 and fired no veto).
# attempt = recent_symbol_counts, every recent plan slot counts (historical,
# byte-identical default); outcome = recent_symbol_failure_counts, W12,
# native-gate deaths only, a publication outranks older failures, plan-stage
# deaths count 0.  STAGED OFF: the proposal-stage veto front-loads the
# decision (hard-reject inside the SAME generation via the single schema
# repair), so a flip changes whether v644's ensemble survives its own audit —
# a first-production-use path for the new semantics.  The live replay (2026-10-30)
# proved zero divergence for v643 itself (sealed _realized_call_equity and
# all three ensemble symbols veto-free under BOTH modes, incl.
# _preflop_spot_adjustment at W6=1/outcome=2), so the flip can land in any
# open window; it waits for the first non-sensitive window with the rest of
# the batch, then one generation of veto-event observation (R3 events
# pipeline.proposal_symbol_ledger_veto / master_plan_audit_direction_veto)
# before it becomes the default.
# POK_DIRECTION_VETO_MODE=outcome
# POK_DIRECTION_VETO_WINDOW=12
# Precommit repair round = 1 (2026-10-22): the 2026-10-19 zero-round setting
# was correct for the OLD behavior, where a repair round replayed the SAME
# frozen seeds (v558/v560/v568/v571/v573 — identical score lines). The gate
# now re-freezes the evaluation plan with a fresh independent one-time nonce
# for the single repair round (tool_eval rotation keyed by
# precommit_rework_count; same opponents/sample depths/thresholds, fixed
# alpha, no retry-until-pass: at most two independent samples per generation).
# 0 restores the immediate circuit breaker; >1 is refused by the pre-registered
# two-sample cap.
POK_MAX_PRECOMMIT_REWORK_ROUNDS=1
# Parent-leg sample depth (2026-10-22 power calibration). Read once at the
# plan-freeze moment and frozen as the parent opponent's own ``matches``.
# Unset = inherit the plan-wide default, which is PRECOMMIT_DEFAULT_N_GAMES=8
# since the 2026-10-21 lowering (not the historical 12). 24 halves the
# parent-outcome score SD and lifts a true-0.55-edge pass rate (strict
# majority: 0.477 at n=8 -> 0.615 at n=24; fair coin 0.3633 -> 0.4194 — the
# old copy's "~0.56 -> ~0.61 / 0.39-0.42" was computed against the n=12
# default) at ~24 extra minutes per precommit. This stays a variance/power
# dial, not an alpha dial: strict majority leaks ~0.36-0.42 under a true tie
# at any of n=8/12/24. Deliberately left unset; the 2026-10-30 breaker
# replay showed the family's failures are threshold+noise, not power, and
# deepening would change zero of the six v635+ verdicts.
# POK_PRECOMMIT_PARENT_N_GAMES=24
